API: SDD

Purpose:
  API testing — verify API endpoints behave correctly according to
  their contracts. API tests validate request/response formats,
  status codes, error handling, and business logic at the API layer.

Owns: ./

Scope:
  REST API endpoints
  GraphQL queries/mutations
  gRPC services
  WebSocket endpoints
  Webhook handlers

Principles:
  Test the contract, not the implementation
  Verify both success and error paths
  Test authentication and authorization
  Test rate limiting and validation
  Test with realistic payloads

Structure:
  Every API test MUST:
    specify the endpoint and method
    define request payload/headers
    define expected response status
    define expected response body
    test error cases

Frameworks:
  Postman/Newman
  REST Assured (Java)
  Supertest (Node)
  Pact (contract testing)
  Schemathesis (property-based)

Navigation:
  Project: @project/project.sdd
  Workflow: @workflow/testing.sdd
  TestLevels: @levels.sdd
  TestTypes: @types.sdd
  TestGates: @gates.sdd
  BDD: @bdd.sdd
  Unit: @unit.sdd
  Integration: @integration.sdd
  Contract: @contract.sdd
